will be the young Ulysses,
son of Laertes.

254
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:14,022
[Tom humming]

255
00:09:14,055 --> 00:09:15,690
Hey, I'm still in here!

256
00:09:15,723 --> 00:09:18,158
NARRATOR:
...bid farewell to their
comrades who have shared

257
00:09:18,192 --> 00:09:20,862
their dangerous adventures
of the last two years.

258
00:09:20,895 --> 00:09:22,797
ALL:
Farewell, comrades.

259
00:09:22,830 --> 00:09:24,598
NARRATOR:
...dauntless pilot
of the Argonauts.

260
00:09:24,632 --> 00:09:25,867
TOM:
And master of knots.

261
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,568
CROW:
Thinks he looks like
Walter Matthau.

262
00:09:28,602 --> 00:09:31,305
NARRATOR:
Laertes,
the restless ruler of Ithaca...

263
00:09:31,338 --> 00:09:33,340
JOEL:
Goes through a lot
of skin bronzer.

264
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:35,342
NARRATOR:
Argo,
who constructed the ship

265
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:37,678
that's served them all so well.

266
00:09:37,712 --> 00:09:39,380
- You bring to Thebes
the most beautiful girl

267
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,480
in... [indistinct]

268
00:09:40,513 --> 00:09:41,482
CROW:
Thank you, Feces.

269
00:09:41,515 --> 00:09:43,550
TOM:
Certainly, Hideous.

270
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,020
- I'd love to see if anyone
can put him in chains.

271
00:09:46,053 --> 00:09:48,755
[All commentators
groaning and whistling]

272
00:09:51,092 --> 00:09:53,060
- I ask you this one favor.

273
00:09:53,093 --> 00:09:55,395
Because I feel
your judgment is mature.

274
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:58,032
JOEL:
Is the horse talking?

275
00:09:58,065 --> 00:09:59,967
- Ulysses is only a child
who thinks he's a man...

276
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,668
[Tom makes baby sounds]

277
00:10:04,172 --> 00:10:05,338
- I think he knows.

278
00:10:05,372 --> 00:10:06,340
You'll behave?

279
00:10:06,373 --> 00:10:07,342
TOM:
Jeff Goldblum!

280
00:10:07,375 --> 00:10:08,442
- ...it's only father.

281
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:09,643
- Now, you listen to me.

282
00:10:09,677 --> 00:10:11,778
- Excuse me,
but you don't have to worry.

283
00:10:11,812 --> 00:10:13,447
- There, you see?
He has no respect.

284
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,615
- What are these?

285
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:15,615
TOM:
Hey, no respect.

286
00:10:15,648 --> 00:10:16,917
Herodicus Dangerfieldicus.

287
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,318
- ...use one of these.

288
00:10:18,352 --> 00:10:20,888
Carefully tie a message
to the leg of a pigeon

289
00:10:20,922 --> 00:10:22,055
and he'll bring it to me.

290
00:10:22,088 --> 00:10:23,857
- But what are you doing
with my pigeons here?

291
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:27,327
A present, they were hers,
Penelope got them at Samos.

292
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,528
- That's true.

293
00:10:28,562 --> 00:10:30,363
And they'll always fly back
to Ithaca

294
00:10:30,397 --> 00:10:31,965
no matter
where you release them.

295
00:10:31,998 --> 00:10:33,733
CROW:
What if you release them
in Ithaca?

296
00:10:33,767 --> 00:10:35,803
- ...discover that these pigeons
can transport the news

297
00:10:35,837 --> 00:10:37,605
quicker than we can,
you will see

298
00:10:37,638 --> 00:10:39,573
that the world
will be very different.

299
00:10:39,607 --> 00:10:40,573
- It's only that
most of us feel

300
00:10:40,607 --> 00:10:42,443
your pigeons are better to eat.

301
00:10:42,477 --> 00:10:44,245
[Laughing]

302
00:10:44,278 --> 00:10:45,478
- Farewell, Hercules.

303
00:10:45,512 --> 00:10:46,513
TOM:
I don't get it.

304
00:10:46,547 --> 00:10:48,648
- Take care of my son.

305
00:10:48,682 --> 00:10:51,485
- Is it my wife
you're interested in too, or me?

306
00:10:51,518 --> 00:10:52,620
Here she is.

307
00:10:52,653 --> 00:10:53,787
JOEL:
Let's bring her out again.

308
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,322
[All commentators
whistling and clapping]

309
00:10:55,355 --> 00:10:56,823
- Come, help me up.

310
00:10:56,857 --> 00:10:58,058
- Oh, I almost forgot.

311
00:10:58,092 --> 00:10:59,060
TOM:
Underwear.

312
00:10:59,093 --> 00:11:00,160
You need it.

313
00:11:00,193 --> 00:11:01,462
- This lute,
it's from Orpheus.

314
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:02,697
- Who's that for?

315
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:04,598
- If you expect to play
the lute with those hands.

316
00:11:04,632 --> 00:11:05,665
[Laughing]

317
00:11:05,698 --> 00:11:06,967
It's for your wife.

318
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,170
TOM:
Liar, liar, lutes on fire.

319
00:11:09,203 --> 00:11:10,772
[Chuckles]

320
00:11:10,805 --> 00:11:12,338
JOEL:
Looks like a giant egg cutter.

321
00:11:15,075 --> 00:11:18,212
TOM:
I was gonna read
on the trip, but...

322
00:11:18,245 --> 00:11:19,613
- Please thank him for me.

323
00:11:19,647 --> 00:11:20,647
- Of course.

324
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:24,918
TOM:
Throw this in the box marked
garage sale.

325
00:11:30,557 --> 00:11:32,258
- Farewell, Ulysses.

326
00:11:32,292 --> 00:11:35,395
Heed the teachings of Hercules
because one day you will...

327
00:11:35,428 --> 00:11:36,663
- Goodbye, Father.

328
00:11:36,697 --> 00:11:39,600
CROW:
I know, so I can
get into a good school.

329
00:11:39,633 --> 00:11:42,302
- Hurry, Hercules,
otherwise we'll all be crying.

330
00:11:42,335 --> 00:11:45,305
[Tom crying]

331
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:46,707
- Be careful, my son.

332
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:47,908
- I will, Father!

333
00:11:47,942 --> 00:11:49,008
JOEL:
Boy, it sure would be hard

334
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,610
to leave all that, huh?

335
00:11:50,643 --> 00:11:51,945
TOM:
Have fun storming the castle,

336
00:11:51,978 --> 00:11:53,613
to thine own self be true,

337
00:11:53,647 --> 00:11:56,183
watch out for that curve, whoa!

338
00:11:58,718 --> 00:12:01,488
CROW:
The high Chaparral.

339
00:12:01,522 --> 00:12:02,690
TOM:
♪ Bum bum bum ♪

340
00:12:02,723 --> 00:12:03,923
ALL COMMENTATORS:
♪ Here comes the king ♪

341
00:12:03,957 --> 00:12:06,060
♪ Here comes the
King wu whoa wu... ♪

342
00:12:06,093 --> 00:12:07,060
JOEL:
♪ Here comes... ♪

343
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:08,728
[Tom chuckles]

344
00:12:08,762 --> 00:12:10,097
CROW:
♪ Oh ho the Wells Fargo ♪

345
00:12:10,130 --> 00:12:11,098
Come on, everybody!

346
00:12:11,132 --> 00:12:12,633
♪ Oh ho the Wells-- ♪

347
00:12:12,667 --> 00:12:14,000
Aw. Mean.

348
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:15,602
- Tomorrow we'll see
the city of Thebes.

349
00:12:15,635 --> 00:12:17,270
JOEL:
Oh, big deal, dad.

350
00:12:17,303 --> 00:12:18,938
- We can tell him
all about it.

351
00:12:18,972 --> 00:12:22,108
We want you to know that
we've been listening to you.

352
00:12:22,142 --> 00:12:23,477
We know that the king
is Oedipus...

353
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:24,612
- Who's a fine man.

354
00:12:24,645 --> 00:12:27,113
- And as for Thebes,
it's tremendous.

355
00:12:27,147 --> 00:12:28,515
All spacious and rich.

356
00:12:28,548 --> 00:12:30,783
- And the stadium and the baths
and the palaces,

357
00:12:30,817 --> 00:12:32,620
it must be heaven,
if you listen to Hercules.

358
00:12:32,653 --> 00:12:33,887
TOM:
And the baths and the malls

359
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,288
and the baths and the...

360
00:12:35,322 --> 00:12:36,457
- I don't know
what you're joking about.

361
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:37,692
TOM:
I don't get it.

362
00:12:37,725 --> 00:12:39,227
- Now you'll see
what a real city's like.

363
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,560
Why, you'll hardly
believe your eyes.

364
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:41,995
JOEL:
They've got sports bars,
you know?

365
00:12:42,028 --> 00:12:43,363
- ...courtesy
of the people alone.

366
00:12:43,397 --> 00:12:44,432
JOEL:
And the baths!

367
00:12:44,465 --> 00:12:45,498
TOM:
Hey.

368
00:12:45,532 --> 00:12:47,167
Hmm?

369
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:50,037
- [indistinct] people,
bristling with anger.

370
00:12:50,070 --> 00:12:51,472
CROW:
Who are those guys?

371
00:12:52,773 --> 00:12:53,807
TOM:
Spartan jerks.

372
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,108
[Coughing]

373
00:12:55,142 --> 00:12:57,077
- ...Thebans, and their manners
are most exquisite.

374
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,445
- They're Argives.

375
00:12:58,478 --> 00:12:59,647
What are they doing in Attica?

376
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,082
CROW: A nickel.
- Why worry about it.

377
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,550
- The Argives are fighters.

378
00:13:03,583 --> 00:13:04,952
They live on war.

379
00:13:04,985 --> 00:13:06,320
They thrive on massacres.

380
00:13:06,353 --> 00:13:07,855
- But wasn't their
commander a Theban?

381
00:13:07,888 --> 00:13:09,022
Let's go a little faster.

382
00:13:09,055 --> 00:13:10,290
- I'll show them!

383
00:13:10,323 --> 00:13:12,158
CROW:
Do you want to go faster?

384
00:13:12,192 --> 00:13:14,228
TOM:
Whoo!

385
00:13:14,262 --> 00:13:15,930
- Hercules,
the ceremony you went through,

386
00:13:15,963 --> 00:13:18,698
the bonds of matrimony,
now you're married.

387
00:13:18,732 --> 00:13:20,100
So, drive carefully.

388
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,837
- I'm grateful, Ulysses,
thanks for the reminder.

389
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:24,538
CROW: But shut up.
- Ho.

390
00:13:27,608 --> 00:13:28,575
Ho.

391
00:13:28,608 --> 00:13:29,577
CROW:
Who you calling "ho?"

392
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:30,577
- So that's the way it is.

393
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:32,145
You're playing games with me?

394
00:13:32,178 --> 00:13:34,215
Alright then, have your fun.

395
00:13:34,248 --> 00:13:36,683
I want to rest.

396
00:13:36,717 --> 00:13:38,152
TOM:
He ran out of body grease

397
00:13:38,185 --> 00:13:39,587
and he gets all crabby.

398
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:42,055
- Huh! Huh!

399
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:43,090
CROW:
Conkacha.

400
00:13:43,123 --> 00:13:45,092
- Go to sleep a bit.

401
00:13:45,125 --> 00:13:47,293
CROW:
Gee, looks like
Poppin' Fresh muffins.

402
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:48,262
TOM:
All buttery.

403
00:13:51,598 --> 00:13:53,433
JOEL:
He's talking to himself.

404
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:59,038
[Crow hums "smoke on the water"
by deep purple]

405
00:13:59,072 --> 00:14:00,507
[Harp plays]

406
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:04,645
JOEL:
♪ In the jungle
The mighty jungle the... ♪

407
00:14:06,713 --> 00:14:11,952
TOM:
♪ We all went down to Montreux ♪

408
00:14:11,985 --> 00:14:15,957
- ♪ Love was in those eyes ♪

409
00:14:15,990 --> 00:14:18,392
TOM:
♪ Hercules couldn't perform ♪

410
00:14:18,425 --> 00:14:19,660
CROW:
Shut up about that.

411
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:21,695
TOM:
- ♪ 'Cause he's using steroids ♪

412
00:14:21,728 --> 00:14:24,365
CROW:
I am not.

413
00:14:24,398 --> 00:14:26,400
She's using
the Mel Bay method.

414
00:14:28,835 --> 00:14:32,072
- ♪ Remain your words to me ♪

415
00:14:32,105 --> 00:14:33,740
JOEL:
Thank you, next!

416
00:14:34,975 --> 00:14:37,645
CROW:
Mrs. Partridge, mom-hmm.

417
00:14:37,678 --> 00:14:45,385
- ♪ Tell me in the skylight
Last night... ♪

418
00:14:45,418 --> 00:14:46,887
TOM:
Sounds like a Western.

419
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,888
- ♪ I was in your arms ♪

420
00:14:48,922 --> 00:14:50,323
CROW:
Hey, this is a family show.

421
00:14:50,357 --> 00:14:54,127
TOM:
Hey, the Herc is
trying to sleep back here.

422
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:59,533
- ♪ ...the evening star
I will walk... ♪

423
00:15:01,468 --> 00:15:03,403
[All howling like wolves]

424
00:15:06,007 --> 00:15:08,408
JOEL:
She's gonna crack her makeup.

425
00:15:08,442 --> 00:15:14,113
- ♪ Just you and I
By the evening star ♪

426
00:15:14,147 --> 00:15:16,083
CROW:
Think I'll fall on my spear,
heh heh.

427
00:15:16,117 --> 00:15:19,052
[♪♪♪]

428
00:15:22,823 --> 00:15:24,223
- Hey.

429
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:25,425
Hey!

430
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:26,527
Stop a moment, stranger.

431
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,728
JOEL:
Our we at grandma's?

432
00:15:27,762 --> 00:15:29,128
- ...mine.

433
00:15:29,162 --> 00:15:31,765
And no one passes through
this valley unless I say so,

434
00:15:31,798 --> 00:15:33,633
and they pay a price.

435
00:15:33,667 --> 00:15:34,635
CROW:
Anthony Quinn?

436
00:15:34,668 --> 00:15:36,370
- ...this valley is Antaeus's.

437
00:15:36,403 --> 00:15:39,272
And you'll do anything
because I say so.

438
00:15:39,305 --> 00:15:40,707
TOM:
Ooo! Ooo, ow.

439
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:42,008
Alright, go ahead.

440
00:15:42,042 --> 00:15:43,210
- Now, tell me.

441
00:15:43,243 --> 00:15:46,280
Do you have any gold
hidden in the carriage?

442
00:15:46,313 --> 00:15:48,415
And the first thing
I'll take are your horses,

443
00:15:48,448 --> 00:15:50,683
so unharness them for me.

444
00:15:50,717 --> 00:15:52,418
- Hercules?
Hercules?

445
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:53,820
- Oh, I want to sleep.

446
00:15:53,853 --> 00:15:55,422
CROW:
Oh, thanks, Hercu-wuss.

447
00:15:55,455 --> 00:15:57,323
- Come on, you. Get down,
I said I want the horses.

448
00:15:57,357 --> 00:15:59,493
- You take advantage of us
just because you're Antaeus.

449
00:15:59,527 --> 00:16:00,560
- And why not?

450
00:16:00,593 --> 00:16:02,228
Just a boy and a lady.

451
00:16:02,262 --> 00:16:03,297
Come on now!
Get down.

452
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,465
- I'll show you
what a boy can do.

453
00:16:04,498 --> 00:16:06,367
CROW:
I can fly!

454
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,633
[Groans]

455
00:16:07,667 --> 00:16:08,802
JOEL:
Nice recovery.

456
00:16:10,203 --> 00:16:11,805
- Hercules, he'll kill him.

457
00:16:11,838 --> 00:16:14,542
- I'm so sleepy,
I can't seem to keep awake.

458
00:16:14,575 --> 00:16:17,343
TOM:
That'd be the definition
of sleepy.

459
00:16:17,377 --> 00:16:18,478
- To my husband.

460
00:16:18,512 --> 00:16:20,313
- And what's he doing?

461
00:16:20,347 --> 00:16:21,448
- He was dozing.

462
00:16:21,482 --> 00:16:22,515
- Dozing, was he?

463
00:16:22,548 --> 00:16:23,850
I'll wake him up.

464
00:16:23,883 --> 00:16:25,018
CROW:
I wouldn't do that.

465
00:16:25,052 --> 00:16:26,753
- I know those sleepy husbands,

466
00:16:26,787 --> 00:16:27,888
or is he just frightened?

467
00:16:27,922 --> 00:16:29,957
- He might awaken
when he sees you.

468
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:31,692
- Husband!

469
00:16:31,725 --> 00:16:32,827
JOEL:
You're my Valentine.

470
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,193
- Hey you, husband.

471
00:16:34,227 --> 00:16:36,997
That's right, kiss your lady
goodbye and pass on.

472
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:38,298
I'm adopting the lady.

473
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:39,365
- Is that right?

474
00:16:39,398 --> 00:16:40,633
- Yes, I'm taking her.

475
00:16:40,667 --> 00:16:41,902
That's my pleasure.

476
00:16:41,935 --> 00:16:44,103
I like her very much,
the lady.

477
00:16:44,137 --> 00:16:45,605
- And what does
she say about that?

478
00:16:45,638 --> 00:16:47,808
- She'd like a new husband,
like every woman.

479
00:16:47,842 --> 00:16:49,075
[Laughs]

480
00:16:49,108 --> 00:16:50,477
[Tom chuckles]

481
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,045
CROW:
Awkward moment.

482
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:54,180
- But Hercules...

483
00:16:54,213 --> 00:16:55,182
Hercules!

484
00:16:55,215 --> 00:16:56,183
TOM:
He makes Andre the Giant

485
00:16:56,217 --> 00:16:57,785
look like Paul Newman.

486
00:16:57,818 --> 00:17:00,353
- They all turn out
to be just like that.

487
00:17:00,387 --> 00:17:02,188
Alright,
come on out and fight.

488
00:17:02,222 --> 00:17:03,457
- A pleasure.

489
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:06,260
JOEL:
Ooo, ooo.

490
00:17:06,293 --> 00:17:07,895
TOM:
What would happen
if he really hit him.

491
00:17:09,128 --> 00:17:12,265
JOEL:
Why is he wearing a bathmat?

492
00:17:12,298 --> 00:17:14,267
- Maybe the next time
you'll treat me better.

493
00:17:15,702 --> 00:17:16,937
Come on, let's be on our way.

494
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:18,505
TOM:
Well, break out
the chest grease.

495
00:17:18,538 --> 00:17:19,773
[Laughs]

496
00:17:19,807 --> 00:17:20,773
JOEL:
He always sees

497
00:17:20,807 --> 00:17:21,975
the bright side of everything.

498
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:23,277
[Tom chuckling]

499
00:17:24,945 --> 00:17:26,380
- You've got a tough skin.

500
00:17:30,217 --> 00:17:31,185
- Hey!

501
00:17:31,218 --> 00:17:32,820
[Grunting]

502
00:17:32,853 --> 00:17:35,988
CROW:
Lambada, the Forbidden Dance.

503
00:17:36,022 --> 00:17:38,958
TOM:
You know, I had a dream
like this once.

504
00:17:38,992 --> 00:17:41,027
JOEL:
Watch it,
I'm wearing my retainer.

505
00:17:42,662 --> 00:17:43,630
TOM:
Lower...

506
00:17:43,663 --> 00:17:44,798
[GRUNTS]
You got it, ah.

507
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,035
Chiropractors.

508
00:17:48,068 --> 00:17:50,670
[Heavy breathing]

509
00:17:50,703 --> 00:17:53,207
[Grunts]

510
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:57,343
[Tom imitates grunting]

511
00:17:57,377 --> 00:18:00,480
JOEL:
I saw Lucy do this
to Mr. Mooney once.

512
00:18:02,682 --> 00:18:04,685
CROW:
Oh! I fell on my keys.

513
00:18:08,122 --> 00:18:09,322
TOM:
Who knows, is this a half nelson

514
00:18:09,355 --> 00:18:10,390
or a full nelson?

515
00:18:10,423 --> 00:18:11,858
CROW:
Uh, looks like a Ricky Nelson.

516
00:18:11,892 --> 00:18:13,993
JOEL:
No, it's his kids,
it's just Nelson.

517
00:18:16,730 --> 00:18:17,697
CROW:
What scares me

518
00:18:17,730 --> 00:18:18,898
is they don't have showers.

519
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:21,100
JOEL:
Okay, you can have me.

520
00:18:21,133 --> 00:18:22,368
I give up.

521
00:18:22,402 --> 00:18:24,437
[Grunting]

522
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,042
TOM:
Rondo Hatton!

523
00:18:29,075 --> 00:18:30,510
JOEL:
You know Rondo's good

524
00:18:30,543 --> 00:18:33,947
'cause you can
slam him down hard.

525
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:34,948
See?

526
00:18:34,982 --> 00:18:36,183
TOM:
Yeah, like that.

527
00:18:36,217 --> 00:18:39,418
CROW:
Whoa, I see London,
I see France...

528
00:18:39,452 --> 00:18:40,853
huh?

529
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:44,090
[Laughs]

530
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,092
TOM:
Oh.

531
00:18:45,125 --> 00:18:46,227
CROW:
Snicker-snag on him,

532
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:48,462
dangle spit,
come on, Herc!

533
00:18:48,495 --> 00:18:49,697
TOM:
I'd bite his nipple.

534
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:51,097
Any questions?

535
00:18:52,532 --> 00:18:53,867
- Come on, Iole.

536
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,202
[Laughs]

537
00:18:55,235 --> 00:18:56,303
TOM:
There he goes.

538
00:18:56,337 --> 00:18:57,470
CROW:
Yeah, I wish he was on our side.

539
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:58,638
He seems really fun.

540
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:01,975
- He might be a god.

541
00:19:02,008 --> 00:19:03,143
- I don't care if he's Pluto.

542
00:19:03,177 --> 00:19:04,510
TOM:
Paul Pluto?

543
00:19:04,543 --> 00:19:05,512
- I'm going to knock
that silly grin off his face

544
00:19:05,545 --> 00:19:06,980
once and for all.

545
00:19:07,013 --> 00:19:09,315
- The god of spice?
[TOM CHUCKLES]

546
00:19:09,348 --> 00:19:11,885
[Grunting]

547
00:19:11,918 --> 00:19:13,120
- I tell you, Hercules,

548
00:19:13,153 --> 00:19:15,155
it must be Antaeus,
son of the earth goddess.

549
00:19:15,188 --> 00:19:17,557
When he touches the ground,
he marshals his forces.

550
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:18,692
- So that's it?

551
00:19:18,725 --> 00:19:20,027
Then I'll change
my way of fighting.

552
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:22,628
JOEL:
That's who he said he was.

553
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:23,730
- Let me down!

554
00:19:23,763 --> 00:19:25,865
You just put me down
and you'll see!

555
00:19:25,898 --> 00:19:27,000
TOM:
Put me down, put me down.

556
00:19:27,033 --> 00:19:28,668
Mom, mom!
This isn't fun anymore.

557
00:19:28,702 --> 00:19:29,837
Mom!

558
00:19:29,870 --> 00:19:31,538
- I'll get even with you,
by the gods!

559
00:19:31,572 --> 00:19:32,838
CROW:
I'll spank you.

560
00:19:32,872 --> 00:19:33,907
- Put me down.

561
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:34,908
Let me down!

562
00:19:34,942 --> 00:19:36,175
[Screaming]

563
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:37,677
CROW:
I've got tubes in my ears.

564
00:19:39,245 --> 00:19:40,747
JOEL:
There.

565
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:41,982
Thanks, friend,

566
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:45,785
I haven't showered
since Zeus was a pup.

567
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:47,420
- ...but one day
you'll have to pass through

568
00:19:47,453 --> 00:19:48,822
my valley again!

569
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:50,390
CROW:
Not after they build
the interstate.

570
00:19:53,827 --> 00:19:56,663
TOM:
"The Virginian",
staring James Drury.

571
00:19:56,697 --> 00:19:58,965
Brought to you by Nabisco.

572
00:19:58,998 --> 00:20:00,967
[Imitates clock ticking]

573
00:20:05,272 --> 00:20:07,307
TOM: [WOMAN"S VOICE]
Oh, thanks for beating up
Antaeus,

574
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:09,142
I really didn't want
to be his wife.

575
00:20:09,175 --> 00:20:10,510
- Just a little way further.

576
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,045
CROW:
There's a gas station.

577
00:20:12,078 --> 00:20:14,080
- I hope we'll be able
to rest there.

578
00:20:14,113 --> 00:20:15,448
- I know this forest
very well.

579
00:20:15,482 --> 00:20:18,018
Why shouldn't we,
it's quiet here.

580
00:20:18,052 --> 00:20:19,352
They say the gates
to the inferno

581
00:20:19,385 --> 00:20:20,787
are hidden among its trees.

582
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:21,822
TOM:
On Broadway.

583
00:20:21,855 --> 00:20:23,423
- But Hercules, look!

584
00:20:23,457 --> 00:20:25,025
JOEL:
Oh, they're tailgating up ahead.

585
00:20:25,058 --> 00:20:26,993
It must be a Packard game.

586
00:20:27,027 --> 00:20:29,228
- It's the first time
I ever saw anyone here.

587
00:20:30,763 --> 00:20:31,865
TOM:
Everybody's making out here.

588
00:20:31,898 --> 00:20:32,865
- Oh, I'm getting wet.

589
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:33,832
- Hurry then.

590
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:38,238
CROW:
He's putting a car cover
on a horse?

591
00:20:38,272 --> 00:20:39,238
- Stop, what do you want?

592
00:20:39,272 --> 00:20:40,273
- Let her alone.

593
00:20:40,307 --> 00:20:41,808
She's come to keep us company.

594
00:20:41,842 --> 00:20:43,543
[TOM CHUCKLES]
- You'll soon find out.

595
00:20:43,577 --> 00:20:44,845
Don't worry.

596
00:20:44,878 --> 00:20:46,780
- Now look at that.
She's beginning to fight.

597
00:20:46,813 --> 00:20:48,248
I'd better tame you.

598
00:20:48,282 --> 00:20:50,717
[Tom grunting]

599
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:53,387
JOEL:
Well, he's bald.

600
00:20:54,855 --> 00:20:55,788
CROW:
Not raining there.

601
00:20:58,225 --> 00:20:59,993
TOM:
I'm with the big guy, sorry.

602
00:21:01,828 --> 00:21:03,630
JOEL:
Edward Arnold?

603
00:21:03,663 --> 00:21:04,898
- But wasn't that Hercules?

604
00:21:04,932 --> 00:21:07,333
CROW:
He's shorter than his pictures.

605
00:21:07,367 --> 00:21:08,502
[Laughing]

606
00:21:08,535 --> 00:21:11,103
JOEL:
They're giddy with violence.

607
00:21:11,137 --> 00:21:14,340
TOM:
And then we ducked
into a little café.

608
00:21:14,373 --> 00:21:15,508
- Be quiet.

609
00:21:15,542 --> 00:21:17,210
- You went to... [indistinct]

610
00:21:17,243 --> 00:21:20,747
my own children
plotted to steal my kingdom

611
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,248
and share it between you.

612
00:21:22,282 --> 00:21:25,418
CROW:
Mr. Hoyle, you're late.

613
00:21:25,452 --> 00:21:28,955
- You and your brother have
driven me out of my kingdom.

614
00:21:28,988 --> 00:21:32,025
Only here can I find asylum.

615
00:21:32,058 --> 00:21:34,695
And here I shall die.

616
00:21:34,728 --> 00:21:35,862
- Oedipus...

617
00:21:35,895 --> 00:21:37,097
JOEL:
Cut! Cut.

618
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:38,832
Hercules, please.

619
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,602
- I know that voice.

620
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:45,605
It recalls a time in my life
when I was happier.

621
00:21:45,638 --> 00:21:47,973
CROW:
Look, it's me, Hercules.

622
00:21:48,007 --> 00:21:49,943
[Coughing]

623
00:21:51,778 --> 00:21:54,380
I came at a bad time, didn't I?

624
00:21:54,413 --> 00:21:57,083
- To me, you are
still the faithful Hercules.

625
00:21:57,117 --> 00:21:58,218
- What are you doing here?

626
00:21:58,252 --> 00:22:00,387
JOEL:
I'm Ralph Richardson.

627
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:02,422
- You're Polynices .

628
00:22:02,455 --> 00:22:04,792
CROW:
I remember you from the gym.

629
00:22:04,825 --> 00:22:06,092
- It was not up to me.

630
00:22:06,125 --> 00:22:08,995
My son thought it better
I renounce the throne,

631
00:22:09,028 --> 00:22:11,297
and so at last I did,

632
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:14,802
so that he and his brother
might rule.

633
00:22:14,835 --> 00:22:16,837
CROW:
And do they write? No.

634
00:22:16,870 --> 00:22:18,738
- ...the throne
to his brother.

635
00:22:18,772 --> 00:22:22,542
But now Polynices tells me
that the year is up.

636
00:22:22,575 --> 00:22:24,010
JOEL:
The god of exposition.

637
00:22:24,043 --> 00:22:26,480
- ...it's my turn now
and it's plain to see

638
00:22:26,513 --> 00:22:28,682
just what his brother
wants to do.

639
00:22:28,715 --> 00:22:30,617
TOM:
It's my turn!

640
00:22:30,650 --> 00:22:32,918
- ...he won't
cede to his brother.

641
00:22:32,952 --> 00:22:34,420
He promised to do so,

642
00:22:34,453 --> 00:22:36,155
but now that his year is up,

643
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,790
he has driven his brother away.

644
00:22:37,823 --> 00:22:39,292
JOEL:
In this new car!

645
00:22:39,325 --> 00:22:42,128
[Tom and crow cheering]

646
00:22:42,162 --> 00:22:43,663
- Just politeness.

647
00:22:43,697 --> 00:22:45,532
- I am not going
to be deceived.

648
00:22:45,565 --> 00:22:47,200
I noticed what he wants,

649
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:49,970
to get and keep the throne
with the help of the Argives.

650
00:22:50,003 --> 00:22:51,838
The throne
carries only tragedy.

651
00:22:51,872 --> 00:22:53,573
It can bring no happiness.

652
00:22:53,607 --> 00:22:56,810
And your city will fall
between these two brothers.

653
00:22:56,843 --> 00:22:58,312
CROW:
So, what I'm hearing here,
Polynices,

654
00:22:58,345 --> 00:23:01,582
is you're angry
with your father, hmm?

655
00:23:01,615 --> 00:23:02,715
- ...and it's men
will be slain...

656
00:23:02,748 --> 00:23:04,350
JOEL: Let's go.
- ...and its women,

657
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:06,252
so long as
these two ambitious rulers

658
00:23:06,285 --> 00:23:08,522
get what they want now.

659
00:23:08,555 --> 00:23:10,423
- Now, listen to me, Polynices,

660
00:23:10,457 --> 00:23:12,092
I've known you
since you were a child,

661
00:23:12,125 --> 00:23:13,460
and I respect your father.

662
00:23:13,493 --> 00:23:15,595
Otherwise, I would exact
justice for Thebes.

663
00:23:15,628 --> 00:23:17,863
CROW:
Crossfire, on the left,
Hercules!

664
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:19,165
- ...I'll go to your brother

665
00:23:19,198 --> 00:23:20,400
and try to convince him

666
00:23:20,433 --> 00:23:22,302
to respect the pact you made.

667
00:23:22,335 --> 00:23:23,403
JOEL:
Pact shmact.

668
00:23:23,437 --> 00:23:25,138
- ...noble thought
that you have, Hercules.

669
00:23:25,172 --> 00:23:26,238
TOM:
On paper.

670
00:23:26,272 --> 00:23:28,073
- ...my sons
will listen to no one.

671
00:23:28,107 --> 00:23:29,542
- But Thebes is my city.

672
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:31,010
Will you spare people
this bloodshed?

673
00:23:31,043 --> 00:23:32,945
JOEL:
And we built this city
on rock and roll!

674
00:23:32,978 --> 00:23:36,015
- ...madness of these men,
or I'll believe that I...

675
00:23:36,048 --> 00:23:37,050
ALL COMMENTATORS:
Hercules...

676
00:23:37,083 --> 00:23:39,618
- ...Hercules,
am deserted by the gods!

677
00:23:39,652 --> 00:23:41,488
JOEL:
Echo, echo, echo...

678
00:23:42,522 --> 00:23:43,490
- Well, Polynices...

679
00:23:43,523 --> 00:23:44,723
CROW:
Well, I can give you

680
00:23:44,757 --> 00:23:47,127
a small part in the chorus,
but that's all.

681
00:23:48,795 --> 00:23:50,797
TOM:
He can pass the pencil test, eh.

682
00:23:52,065 --> 00:23:53,367
- If it's better.

683
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,102
Go Eteocles, go on.

684
00:23:55,135 --> 00:23:56,168
I grant you six days

685
00:23:56,202 --> 00:23:57,937
to let me know
if you can make peace.

686
00:23:57,970 --> 00:23:59,172
- At the end of those six days,

687
00:23:59,205 --> 00:24:02,108
we'll march our army
against the Thebans.

688
00:24:10,917 --> 00:24:16,623
- ♪ Heading out to
Eden yeah brother ♪

689
00:24:16,657 --> 00:24:18,958
- Tom, consider the grape.

690
00:24:18,992 --> 00:24:20,627
- Oh, I will.

691
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,428
- So delicate.

692
00:24:22,462 --> 00:24:24,230
So firm.

693
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:25,732
[Gasping]

694
00:24:25,765 --> 00:24:27,200
- You guys, I don't see why
I have to be the one

695
00:24:27,233 --> 00:24:28,368
to peel these grapes.

696
00:24:28,402 --> 00:24:29,768
You know, it's really
kind of hard.

697
00:24:29,802 --> 00:24:31,805
- And he calls
himself a hedonist.

698
00:24:31,838 --> 00:24:33,307
[Laughing]

699
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:34,607
- Well, you know what?

700
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:36,442
I think it's great
that Gypsy built this set

701
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:38,010
and made these costumes for us

702
00:24:38,043 --> 00:24:39,312
just so she could put on a show.

703
00:24:39,345 --> 00:24:41,648
You guys should do
something like that.

704
00:24:41,682 --> 00:24:42,915
- You know, you're right.

705
00:24:42,948 --> 00:24:44,650
Starting right now,

706
00:24:44,683 --> 00:24:47,387
I'm gonna roll over
and eat more grapes.

707
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:48,422
- Ah.

708
00:24:48,455 --> 00:24:49,422
- Oh, here she comes.

709
00:24:49,455 --> 00:24:50,423
She's beautiful.

710
00:24:50,457 --> 00:24:51,925
- Hey, looking good, Gypsy.

711
00:24:51,958 --> 00:24:53,125
- Thank you.

712
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:56,195
And now
for a little song in G.

713
00:24:56,228 --> 00:24:57,297
[Clears throat]

714
00:24:57,330 --> 00:25:00,067
♪ Last night... ♪

715
00:25:00,100 --> 00:25:02,135
- Her gown is like
a beautiful breeze.

716
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:03,770
- ♪ Last night... ♪

717
00:25:04,938 --> 00:25:08,140
♪ Last night... ♪

718
00:25:08,173 --> 00:25:11,243
- So, what's
she supposed to be, Joel?

719
00:25:11,277 --> 00:25:13,513
- I'm the Hellenistic ideal.

720
00:25:13,547 --> 00:25:15,548
- ♪ Last night... ♪

721
00:25:15,582 --> 00:25:16,750
- You know, folks,
you just don't hear

722
00:25:16,783 --> 00:25:18,818
music like that anymore.

723
00:25:18,852 --> 00:25:20,153
- You know, folks,

724
00:25:20,187 --> 00:25:22,488
I have a feeling
this is gonna go on like this,

725
00:25:22,522 --> 00:25:24,757
so why don't you
run on ahead to the commercial.

726
00:25:24,790 --> 00:25:26,225
We'll catch up...

727
00:25:26,258 --> 00:25:29,295
- ♪ Last night I couldn't
Get to sleep at all... ♪

728
00:25:29,328 --> 00:25:30,697
- Hey, Joel?

729
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:33,533
Am I the only one that notices
I'm not eating a grape?

730
00:25:35,735 --> 00:25:38,672
[♪♪♪]

731
00:25:43,075 --> 00:25:45,278
JOEL:
That was good.

732
00:25:45,312 --> 00:25:47,813
TOM:
[indistinct].

733
00:25:47,847 --> 00:25:49,415
- Welcome to my house,
Eteocles.

734
00:25:49,448 --> 00:25:51,550
CROW:
Two words, Hercules,
"French doors."

735
00:25:51,583 --> 00:25:52,552
- ...the lady with you?

736
00:25:52,585 --> 00:25:53,720
- No,
Ulysses will come with me.

737
00:25:53,753 --> 00:25:54,720
CROW:
Same thing.

738
00:25:54,753 --> 00:25:56,422
- Ulysses?
Ulysses, now who is he?

739
00:25:56,455 --> 00:25:59,192
- Ulysses, son of Laertes,
King of Ithaca.

740
00:25:59,225 --> 00:26:00,360
- A king without soldiers?

741
00:26:00,393 --> 00:26:01,460
I'm not interested.

742
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:03,963
Take this.

743
00:26:03,997 --> 00:26:04,965
TOM:
Put it where
the sun don't shine.

744
00:26:04,998 --> 00:26:05,965
- You can tell my brother
this.

745
00:26:05,998 --> 00:26:07,367
From now on,
what he asks I will do.

746
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,735
JOEL:
You've been lifting,
what's your max?

747
00:26:08,768 --> 00:26:10,670
- That's what
you're here for, isn't it?

748
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:13,940
And tomorrow morning,

749
00:26:13,973 --> 00:26:15,275
I'll send servants,
goods, and provisions.

750
00:26:15,308 --> 00:26:16,375
CROW:
And lawyers, guns and money.

751
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:18,745
- If you live alone
here in Thebes,

752
00:26:18,778 --> 00:26:19,812
you'll grow impatient.

753
00:26:19,845 --> 00:26:20,813
TOM:
Need a roommate?

754
00:26:20,847 --> 00:26:22,048
- Thank you.

755
00:26:22,082 --> 00:26:23,417
- I'll guard Iole,
'til he gets home.

756
00:26:23,450 --> 00:26:25,652
- Aw, then I'm certain
she'll be alright.

757
00:26:25,685 --> 00:26:27,020
CROW: Ouch.
JOEL: Grrr.

758
00:26:27,053 --> 00:26:31,190
- Creon is the purest and most
intelligent man in Thebes.

759
00:26:31,223 --> 00:26:32,792
TOM:
And Creon's nontoxic.

760
00:26:32,825 --> 00:26:34,093
- ...in his way.

761
00:26:34,127 --> 00:26:35,428
I bid you goodbye.

762
00:26:35,462 --> 00:26:37,197
[Laughs]

