1015
00:36:48,473 --> 00:36:50,843
I hope she's in a body stocking.

1016
00:36:50,877 --> 00:36:52,478
JOEL:
Ordinary pantyhose are okay

1017
00:36:52,512 --> 00:36:56,382
under funky clothes
but gentlemen prefer Hanes.

1018
00:36:57,817 --> 00:36:59,885
CROW:
Ooo.

1019
00:36:59,918 --> 00:37:02,922
[Tom imitates music]

1020
00:37:06,292 --> 00:37:07,427
All snaky like.

1021
00:37:07,460 --> 00:37:09,428
CROW: Where'd she go?
TOM: Huh? Huh?

1022
00:37:09,462 --> 00:37:11,097
CROW:
Oh, there she is.

1023
00:37:12,898 --> 00:37:14,367
TOM:
Oh, like who can't do that?

1024
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:15,668
CROW:
Oh, I'm standing on my head.

1025
00:37:15,702 --> 00:37:17,002
Could somebody help me?

1026
00:37:25,277 --> 00:37:27,480
TOM:
So, does this thing
heat up at all?

1027
00:37:27,513 --> 00:37:29,848
JOEL:
Hey, this is not
my beautiful house.

1028
00:37:29,882 --> 00:37:31,450
This is not my beautiful wife.

1029
00:37:31,483 --> 00:37:33,885
How did I get here?

1030
00:37:33,918 --> 00:37:36,922
CROW:
Ah, the chicken dance,
very nice.

1031
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:43,462
JOEL:
That's what I did in my act.

1032
00:37:45,798 --> 00:37:46,765
CROW:
Hey, wait a minute.

1033
00:37:46,798 --> 00:37:47,767
Her skin has a zipper.

1034
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:48,800
TOM:
Ooo.

1035
00:37:51,503 --> 00:37:53,705
ALL:
Timber!

1036
00:37:56,542 --> 00:37:58,243
JOEL:
Let's see, it snowed real bad

1037
00:37:58,277 --> 00:37:59,545
and we got snowed in

1038
00:37:59,578 --> 00:38:03,048
and Murray had to stay over,
and then...

1039
00:38:04,550 --> 00:38:06,185
CROW:
This is jogging my memory.

1040
00:38:06,218 --> 00:38:07,285
TOM:
It's jogging something.

1041
00:38:07,318 --> 00:38:08,353
[Chuckles]

1042
00:38:08,387 --> 00:38:10,322
- Anyway, I like the idea
of being a king.

1043
00:38:12,057 --> 00:38:14,727
By the way, what's my name?

1044
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,728
JOEL:
Who's my daddy?

1045
00:38:15,762 --> 00:38:17,997
Was he rich,
was he rich like me?

1046
00:38:18,030 --> 00:38:20,465
- Nothing,
it's just if you called me...

1047
00:38:21,967 --> 00:38:24,103
- To me, your name is love.

1048
00:38:24,137 --> 00:38:25,103
CROW:
Buddy Love?

1049
00:38:31,210 --> 00:38:34,647
- Ha ha. I'm beginning
to like this place.

1050
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:35,948
- And me.

1051
00:38:35,982 --> 00:38:37,048
TOM:
Eh, you I can take or leave.

1052
00:38:37,082 --> 00:38:38,617
- ...most of all.

1053
00:38:38,650 --> 00:38:42,020
JOEL:
Hey, 2,000 years,
that'll be worth something.

1054
00:38:44,257 --> 00:38:45,290
TOM:
What are you doing?

1055
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:48,627
Ooo, you taste like Diogenes.

1056
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:50,228
What're they up to, Joel?

1057
00:38:50,262 --> 00:38:52,097
CROW:
Uh, let's pack it up, girls.

1058
00:38:52,130 --> 00:38:53,965
Our work here is finished.

1059
00:38:56,102 --> 00:39:00,105
TOM: Tada.
CROW: Mmm, bless this mess?

1060
00:39:00,138 --> 00:39:01,073
Huh.

1061
00:39:06,212 --> 00:39:08,780
TOM:
Hey, this is the girl's dorm.

1062
00:39:08,813 --> 00:39:10,582
JOEL:
Aw, this is really cute, Karen,

1063
00:39:10,615 --> 00:39:12,552
can I borrow it sometime?

1064
00:39:15,420 --> 00:39:16,388
CROW:
Hey, all the boys

1065
00:39:16,422 --> 00:39:18,690
have to register
at the front desk.

1066
00:39:18,723 --> 00:39:20,492
- What's in the bottom
of the chest?

1067
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:22,495
Does it mean anything
for you or Hercules?

1068
00:39:22,528 --> 00:39:24,697
CROW:
What's that supposed to mean?

1069
00:39:24,730 --> 00:39:26,698
- Will you be still?

1070
00:39:26,732 --> 00:39:28,367
JOEL:
Gonna cry now, baby?

1071
00:39:30,002 --> 00:39:31,437
- When is he coming?

1072
00:39:31,470 --> 00:39:33,405
- He's only been gone
about three days.

1073
00:39:33,438 --> 00:39:34,640
- Because of this treaty,
you know.

1074
00:39:34,673 --> 00:39:35,740
They need time.

1075
00:39:35,773 --> 00:39:37,175
You can't settle them
right away.

1076
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:40,512
- Yes, I see. If he's delayed,
it's only logical.

1077
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:42,748
But I feel so anxious
when I don't hear.

1078
00:39:42,782 --> 00:39:43,748
JOEL:
We should have at least

1079
00:39:43,782 --> 00:39:44,950
gotten a pigeon by now.

1080
00:39:44,983 --> 00:39:46,518
- I'll stay
only until tomorrow morning

1081
00:39:46,552 --> 00:39:49,322
and then I'll go to see
if I can locate him.

1082
00:39:49,355 --> 00:39:52,858
TOM:
I'll call the finder
of lost loves.

1083
00:39:52,892 --> 00:39:54,927
CROW:
All of a sudden
it's paint your wagon.

1084
00:39:58,030 --> 00:39:59,198
All:
[Singing "one tin soldier"]

1085
00:39:59,232 --> 00:40:03,002
♪ Peace on earth
Was all it said... ♪

1086
00:40:03,035 --> 00:40:04,803
TOM: [CLAPPING]
Do do do!

1087
00:40:04,837 --> 00:40:06,572
CROW:
Hey, I can see
my house from here.

1088
00:40:09,208 --> 00:40:10,910
TOM:
Bird loves, woo!

1089
00:40:12,377 --> 00:40:14,713
CROW:
I thought I saw Ulythes...

1090
00:40:14,747 --> 00:40:16,982
I did, I did see Ulythes.

1091
00:40:18,217 --> 00:40:19,452
TOM:
Hey, you guys wait here.

1092
00:40:28,027 --> 00:40:29,027
JOEL:
I was just doing the dishes.

1093
00:40:29,060 --> 00:40:30,262
[Hums]

1094
00:40:30,295 --> 00:40:32,598
- Come on, now.
You're going to work, now!

1095
00:40:32,632 --> 00:40:34,733
JOEL:
I gotta finish
these dishes first.

1096
00:40:41,273 --> 00:40:43,608
TOM:
You're... hurting...

1097
00:40:43,642 --> 00:40:47,780
- My boy, I've discovered
something very important.

1098
00:40:47,813 --> 00:40:49,013
TOM:
This really bugs me.

1099
00:40:49,047 --> 00:40:52,217
- Up to now, I've been making
one big mistake.

1100
00:40:52,250 --> 00:40:53,985
CROW:
Hey, is he turtle waxing him?

1101
00:40:54,018 --> 00:40:56,322
- And stay awake at night.

1102
00:40:56,355 --> 00:40:59,425
Otherwise you'll lose
the best part of your life.

1103
00:40:59,458 --> 00:41:01,127
JOEL:
I can see you've been real--

1104
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:03,362
really thinking deep here, sir.

1105
00:41:06,998 --> 00:41:08,233
TOM:
Hey, it's Ting.

1106
00:41:08,267 --> 00:41:10,202
You know that's hard
to find around here.

1107
00:41:13,972 --> 00:41:14,973
- Is it prepared?

1108
00:41:18,910 --> 00:41:22,748
CROW:
Mmm, dinner, Herc.

1109
00:41:22,782 --> 00:41:25,217
- Ah, yes.
The night was made for love.

1110
00:41:25,250 --> 00:41:26,685
JOEL:
And Michelob.

1111
00:41:28,053 --> 00:41:30,555
- The sun out there
dulls the senses.

1112
00:41:31,957 --> 00:41:34,993
Enough.
I'm hungry.

1113
00:41:35,027 --> 00:41:36,862
TOM:
Well, I think you just
insulted the waitress.

1114
00:41:36,895 --> 00:41:40,465
- Ha ha.
What a life.

1115
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:42,602
You wake up in the morning
without a care in the world

1116
00:41:42,635 --> 00:41:43,968
and nothing to do.

1117
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:46,638
CROW:
Just like collecting
unemployment checks.

1118
00:41:48,940 --> 00:41:51,010
TOM:
What the heck ya doing there?

1119
00:41:51,043 --> 00:41:53,178
- Clumsy!

1120
00:41:53,212 --> 00:41:54,847
It looks like
you did it on purpose.

1121
00:41:56,382 --> 00:41:58,983
JOEL:
Shhh, let's play charades.

1122
00:42:00,085 --> 00:42:02,888
CROW:
Okay, I'll go along.

1123
00:42:02,922 --> 00:42:04,357
ALL COMMENTATORS:
Look to the left,

1124
00:42:04,390 --> 00:42:05,557
look to the right,

1125
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:08,227
stand up, sit down,
and fight fight fight!

1126
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,230
CROW:
This is the
fountain of dorkiness.

1127
00:42:12,263 --> 00:42:14,267
TOM:
Eh, got any ketchup for this?

1128
00:42:16,835 --> 00:42:18,637
CROW:
Don't tell.

1129
00:42:18,670 --> 00:42:20,372
- You are Hercules.

1130
00:42:20,405 --> 00:42:21,607
ALL COMMENTATORS:
Thbbbt!

1131
00:42:24,075 --> 00:42:25,978
- What did you say?
TOM: I forgot already.

1132
00:42:26,012 --> 00:42:27,045
- Hercules.

1133
00:42:27,078 --> 00:42:28,280
TOM:
Uh-huh.

1134
00:42:28,313 --> 00:42:29,648
- Hercules?

1135
00:42:29,682 --> 00:42:31,650
What about Hercules?

1136
00:42:31,683 --> 00:42:33,018
- Iole.

1137
00:42:33,052 --> 00:42:35,220
- Go away.
I don't understand a thing.

1138
00:42:35,253 --> 00:42:36,855
TOM:
Mmm-hmm.

1139
00:42:36,888 --> 00:42:38,290
- Iole, your marriage,
Eteocles,

1140
00:42:38,323 --> 00:42:39,625
Polynises, the message...

1141
00:42:39,658 --> 00:42:42,360
TOM:
Uh, uh, things you'd say
to Socrates.

1142
00:42:49,267 --> 00:42:50,402
- Bend it.

1143
00:42:50,435 --> 00:42:51,870
If you can't,
you'll convince me.

1144
00:42:51,903 --> 00:42:54,072
CROW:
If you can, you're Uri Geller.

1145
00:42:54,105 --> 00:42:57,242
JOEL:
You're lucky
I'm in a good mood, Ulysses.

1146
00:42:57,275 --> 00:42:59,612
[Grunting]

1147
00:43:07,052 --> 00:43:08,620
CROW:
Oh, rats. I can't bend it.

1148
00:43:08,653 --> 00:43:11,490
Guess I have to stay here
with all the nymphs.

1149
00:43:18,830 --> 00:43:20,232
TOM:
Hit the road, Pedro.

1150
00:43:20,265 --> 00:43:22,533
Oh, hi, Herc.

1151
00:43:22,567 --> 00:43:25,270
[Crow whistles]
[Tom imitates horn music]

1152
00:43:27,707 --> 00:43:28,640
- Good morning.

1153
00:43:33,145 --> 00:43:34,847
- Did you sleep well last night?

1154
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:35,913
- Wonderfully.

1155
00:43:35,947 --> 00:43:37,248
I dreamt of ya.

1156
00:43:39,752 --> 00:43:41,187
- And I'm flattered.

1157
00:43:41,220 --> 00:43:44,022
CROW:
And flattery will
get you everywhere.

1158
00:43:44,055 --> 00:43:46,025
TOM:
Eh, old ball and chain.

1159
00:43:46,058 --> 00:43:48,293
[Chuckles]

1160
00:43:48,327 --> 00:43:49,462
JOEL:
So, what's on the slate today?

1161
00:43:49,495 --> 00:43:51,963
Eatin' and lovin', huh?

1162
00:43:51,997 --> 00:43:54,900
- Somehow, I recall
that you had a different face.

1163
00:43:54,933 --> 00:43:55,933
JOEL:
Yeah, it was Phyllis Diller's,

1164
00:43:55,967 --> 00:43:57,135
I had to return it.

1165
00:43:57,168 --> 00:43:59,203
- No. Just different.

1166
00:43:59,237 --> 00:44:01,773
Blonde hair, sweet smile.

1167
00:44:01,807 --> 00:44:03,108
JOEL:
Hair growing out of your wart.

1168
00:44:03,142 --> 00:44:05,510
- So you've begun to betray me
in your dreams.

1169
00:44:08,247 --> 00:44:11,083
- Aren't you afraid that somehow
we'll displease the fates,

1170
00:44:11,117 --> 00:44:12,650
and they'll take
their revenge on us?

1171
00:44:12,683 --> 00:44:14,285
TOM:
I try not to think about it.

1172
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:16,122
So, anyway.

1173
00:44:18,657 --> 00:44:19,858
JOEL:
Uh, guys? Guys...

1174
00:44:19,892 --> 00:44:20,892
- I don't want to talk
about sad things

1175
00:44:20,925 --> 00:44:22,293
when I'm so happy.

1176
00:44:22,327 --> 00:44:25,063
CROW:
But they're--
something's gonna--

1177
00:44:25,097 --> 00:44:26,065
Joel, what are they...

1178
00:44:26,098 --> 00:44:27,032
TOM:
What they gonna...

1179
00:44:30,102 --> 00:44:33,072
[♪♪♪]

1180
00:44:35,640 --> 00:44:37,708
VOICE ON PA:
This is
the water of forgetfulness.

1181
00:44:37,742 --> 00:44:40,078
Those who drink
of it will forget all.

1182
00:44:40,112 --> 00:44:41,080
- Say, who manufactures

1183
00:44:41,113 --> 00:44:42,447
the water of forgetfulness,
anyway?

1184
00:44:42,480 --> 00:44:44,517
- Oh, it says
here on the bottle...

1185
00:44:44,550 --> 00:44:48,553
Mendota Springs, makers
of the water of forgetfulness

1186
00:44:48,587 --> 00:44:51,657
since-- uh-oh--
let me think--

1187
00:44:51,690 --> 00:44:56,328
oh, it's on the tip
of my tongue-- when was it?

1188
00:44:56,362 --> 00:44:58,297
VOICE ON PA:
This is the carob shake
of pretentiousness.

1189
00:44:58,330 --> 00:44:59,865
- Ooo, let me try that.

1190
00:44:59,898 --> 00:45:02,133
VOICE ON PA:
Those who drink of it will
join theater companies.

1191
00:45:02,167 --> 00:45:04,235
- Yeah, you know, I'm doing
an anti-Columbus thing

1192
00:45:04,268 --> 00:45:06,138
down at the heart of
the Meat Puppet Beast Theater.

1193
00:45:06,172 --> 00:45:07,973
Yeah, it's a real opportunity
for me to stretch.

1194
00:45:08,007 --> 00:45:09,240
- Hey, Joel?

1195
00:45:09,273 --> 00:45:10,275
That cup looks like
it's from Dairy Queen.

1196
00:45:10,308 --> 00:45:11,277
Can I have some?

1197
00:45:11,310 --> 00:45:12,643
- Mmm-hmm.

1198
00:45:12,677 --> 00:45:13,745
VOICE ON PA:
This is the blizzard
of loneliness.

1199
00:45:13,778 --> 00:45:15,147
Those who drink off it

1200
00:45:15,180 --> 00:45:18,050
will sit on the beach wearing
long pants and black socks

1201
00:45:18,083 --> 00:45:20,518
and look for change in the sand
with a metal detector.

1202
00:45:20,552 --> 00:45:22,320
- I found a quarter!

1203
00:45:22,353 --> 00:45:23,288
- Hey, who wants gum?

1204
00:45:23,322 --> 00:45:24,957
ALL: I do, I do!
- Here.

1205
00:45:24,990 --> 00:45:27,225
VOICE ON PA:
You're eating the fruit
striped gum of civility.

1206
00:45:27,258 --> 00:45:29,728
Those who chew it
will get a civil service job

1207
00:45:29,762 --> 00:45:31,028
with good benefits.

1208
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:33,398
- Yup, thanks to the fruit
stripe gum of civility,

1209
00:45:33,432 --> 00:45:35,300
I gotta a good
dental plan now.

1210
00:45:35,333 --> 00:45:36,802
Ironic, huh?

1211
00:45:36,835 --> 00:45:38,770
VOICE ON PA:
You are eating
the green bean and French onion

1212
00:45:38,803 --> 00:45:40,605
casserole of happiness.

1213
00:45:40,638 --> 00:45:42,573
Those who eat off it
will find the serenity

1214
00:45:42,607 --> 00:45:44,408
that only a hot dish can bring.

1215
00:45:44,442 --> 00:45:47,678
- Oh, you know, I really,
really love this stuff.

1216
00:45:47,712 --> 00:45:50,882
It's so nutritious
and it's so good for you

1217
00:45:50,915 --> 00:45:52,583
and I love my location,

1218
00:45:52,617 --> 00:45:55,053
it's so conveniently located.

1219
00:45:55,087 --> 00:45:57,422
What with the [indistinct]
and dinner theater

1220
00:45:57,455 --> 00:45:59,157
and the new high school.

1221
00:45:59,190 --> 00:46:00,692
And oh, the Elks Lodge

1222
00:46:00,725 --> 00:46:04,395
puts on a wonderful fish fry
every weekend.

1223
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:06,932
And we're right next
to the chain of lakes.

1224
00:46:06,965 --> 00:46:08,833
And we've got movie sign,

1225
00:46:08,867 --> 00:46:11,670
and they do the big Chatakwa
show every summer,

1226
00:46:11,703 --> 00:46:13,238
and they've got movie sign...

1227
00:46:13,272 --> 00:46:14,940
ALL:
Movie sign?

1228
00:46:14,973 --> 00:46:16,308
[Yelling]

1229
00:46:25,550 --> 00:46:26,718
TOM:
That dish is filling, isn't it?

1230
00:46:26,752 --> 00:46:28,820
JOEL AND CROW:
Oh, yes. So good.

1231
00:46:28,853 --> 00:46:30,722
CROW:
Hey, Peter, Paul, and Mary.

1232
00:46:30,755 --> 00:46:32,157
- And where did they
find the princess?

1233
00:46:32,190 --> 00:46:33,158
TOM:
The Personals.

1234
00:46:33,192 --> 00:46:35,160
- Just planning to run away

1235
00:46:35,193 --> 00:46:36,728
because
she couldn't stand Thebes,

1236
00:46:36,762 --> 00:46:38,363
and she wanted to rejoin
her husband.

1237
00:46:38,397 --> 00:46:39,430
CROW:
Walk this way.

1238
00:46:41,767 --> 00:46:43,235
Full stop.

1239
00:46:43,268 --> 00:46:45,737
- Did you,
did you hear from Hercules?

1240
00:46:45,770 --> 00:46:47,172
CROW:
Well, just a message
on my machine.

1241
00:46:47,205 --> 00:46:52,010
- ...he's away and all I've done
was wait here alone.

1242
00:46:52,043 --> 00:46:54,980
And if I did run away,
it was only that,

1243
00:46:55,013 --> 00:46:56,882
I beg you
to let me go to Hercules.

1244
00:46:56,915 --> 00:46:59,483
JOEL:
And let me smoke in my room.

1245
00:46:59,517 --> 00:47:02,988
- Reunited under the tender care
of my brother Polynises.

1246
00:47:03,022 --> 00:47:04,657
- I don't see what you mean,
sire.

1247
00:47:04,690 --> 00:47:06,458
- Well, it's not her fault,
Eteocles.

1248
00:47:06,492 --> 00:47:07,858
And why blame Hercules?

1249
00:47:07,892 --> 00:47:09,027
Don't you see?

1250
00:47:09,060 --> 00:47:11,028
If you let them go
to each other, then...

1251
00:47:11,062 --> 00:47:12,030
TOM:
Stop yelling!

1252
00:47:12,063 --> 00:47:13,232
Why is everyone yelling!

1253
00:47:13,265 --> 00:47:14,265
- You talk to me
as if I'm prepared

1254
00:47:14,298 --> 00:47:16,133
to take leave of my senses.

1255
00:47:16,167 --> 00:47:17,368
Take the woman away.

1256
00:47:17,402 --> 00:47:19,070
- But they're posing
for the Primo Beer can.

1257
00:47:19,103 --> 00:47:20,405
TOM AND CROW:
Cool.

1258
00:47:20,438 --> 00:47:22,440
- But that's unjust, inhuman.

1259
00:47:25,210 --> 00:47:27,112
- I shall now arrest
any and all Thebans

1260
00:47:27,145 --> 00:47:29,615
suspected
of plotting with Polynises.

1261
00:47:29,648 --> 00:47:31,148
Arrest them all!
JOEL: They left, sir.

1262
00:47:31,182 --> 00:47:34,853
- With their goods,
and families, and servants.

1263
00:47:34,887 --> 00:47:36,588
JOEL:
Can't we just arrest
everyone in red?

1264
00:47:36,622 --> 00:47:38,857
- You all pretend
that you want justice.

1265
00:47:38,890 --> 00:47:42,393
That nobody Hercules
and my friends here at court.

1266
00:47:42,427 --> 00:47:44,328
TOM:
God!

1267
00:47:44,362 --> 00:47:46,532
- Creon will be my example.

1268
00:47:46,565 --> 00:47:49,300
TOM:
What about [indistinct]?

1269
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:52,070
[All commentators mumbling]

1270
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:56,275
CROW:
Made ya look, ha ha.

1271
00:48:01,980 --> 00:48:03,015
TOM:
And now, a journey

1272
00:48:03,048 --> 00:48:04,015
through the lymph nodes.

1273
00:48:04,048 --> 00:48:05,050
JOEL:
You mean nymph loads.

1274
00:48:05,083 --> 00:48:06,250
TOM:
Oh.

1275
00:48:06,283 --> 00:48:07,852
CROW:
Hey.

1276
00:48:07,885 --> 00:48:09,353
Oh, working on
a new filing system.

1277
00:48:09,387 --> 00:48:11,188
[Laughs]

1278
00:48:11,222 --> 00:48:12,190
Alright.

1279
00:48:12,223 --> 00:48:14,660
TOM:
Oh, oh.

1280
00:48:14,693 --> 00:48:17,997
[Imitates snoring sound]

1281
00:48:18,030 --> 00:48:19,965
- Wake up,
it's time to go to work.

1282
00:48:19,998 --> 00:48:23,035
Get out of bed now.

1283
00:48:23,068 --> 00:48:24,903
CROW:
I can't hear you,
I'm sleeping...

1284
00:48:24,937 --> 00:48:26,505
in death.

1285
00:48:26,538 --> 00:48:28,040
- Get up now, it's late.

1286
00:48:28,073 --> 00:48:29,675
Your master's waiting
for his massage.

1287
00:48:29,708 --> 00:48:31,277
JOEL:
At two in the morning?

1288
00:48:36,047 --> 00:48:38,417
TOM:
Massage this, you cretin.

1289
00:48:38,450 --> 00:48:39,383
I mean, cratin.

1290
00:48:43,088 --> 00:48:45,623
CROW:
Creon will be played
by the bassoon.

1291
00:48:45,657 --> 00:48:47,525
[Tom humming]

1292
00:48:49,160 --> 00:48:50,828
CROW:
What the heck is going on here?

1293
00:48:50,862 --> 00:48:56,568
ALL: [ALONG WITH SOUNDTRACK]
Dum dum dum...

1294
00:48:56,602 --> 00:48:57,568
CROW:
Oh yeah, like no one's

1295
00:48:57,602 --> 00:48:59,603
gonna notice
the string on the lock.

1296
00:48:59,637 --> 00:49:01,640
JOEL:
It's a Hercules
power wrist band.

1297
00:49:01,673 --> 00:49:02,607
CROW:
Nice.

1298
00:49:04,843 --> 00:49:06,645
JOEL: [WHISPERING]
Real nice, fix it up good.

1299
00:49:13,452 --> 00:49:14,452
CROW:
Coming, mom.

1300
00:49:15,653 --> 00:49:16,655
TOM:
Ooo, yeah.

1301
00:49:16,688 --> 00:49:18,590
Big old jelly donut, oh.

1302
00:49:28,333 --> 00:49:31,437
CROW:
You are nuttier than
an outhouse rat, you know that?

1303
00:49:33,872 --> 00:49:35,873
- That's the second time
you knocked over my goblet.

1304
00:49:35,907 --> 00:49:36,875
CROW:
How would he remember that?

1305
00:49:36,908 --> 00:49:39,978
- I do it for you, Hercules.

1306
00:49:40,012 --> 00:49:42,247
- Why is it you keep on
calling me Hercules?

1307
00:49:42,280 --> 00:49:43,782
JOEL:
You know my name is Todd.

1308
00:49:46,317 --> 00:49:49,922
TOM:
Mmm, really tore through
those bear claws, didn't you?

1309
00:49:49,955 --> 00:49:51,390
- ...I've heard
that name before.

1310
00:49:51,423 --> 00:49:52,857
- You'll see.
Soon you'll remember.

1311
00:49:52,890 --> 00:49:54,258
CROW:
Just look at
your chariot license.

1312
00:49:54,292 --> 00:49:56,227
- Too complicated
to explain to you now.

1313
00:49:56,260 --> 00:49:58,197
I beg you to avoid
drinking that water,

1314
00:49:58,230 --> 00:49:59,697
then you'll recover your memory

1315
00:49:59,730 --> 00:50:00,998
and soon
we'll be able to escape.

1316
00:50:01,032 --> 00:50:03,302
JOEL:
Escape from this, why?

1317
00:50:03,335 --> 00:50:05,403
- Isn't this your native land?

1318
00:50:05,437 --> 00:50:07,372
TOM:
Uh, Herc, I think you're getting

1319
00:50:07,405 --> 00:50:08,773
your appointments
mixed up there.

1320
00:50:08,807 --> 00:50:11,008
- ...comrades. We were
captured and brought here.

1321
00:50:11,042 --> 00:50:13,145
I tell you that
we must get out of here.

1322
00:50:13,178 --> 00:50:14,847
What I saw was so terrible.

1323
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:16,313
JOEL:
Curly Sue?

1324
00:50:16,347 --> 00:50:19,083
- You see, during the day,
they don't bother me.

1325
00:50:19,117 --> 00:50:22,020
At night, I'm put into a cell
and locked inside.

1326
00:50:22,053 --> 00:50:23,955
Yesterday, I was looking
for a means to get out.

1327
00:50:23,988 --> 00:50:25,023
CROW:
That's Dippity-Do.

1328
00:50:25,057 --> 00:50:27,058
- ...I saw a path
leading to a cave.

1329
00:50:27,092 --> 00:50:28,593
TOM:
Here, let me demonstrate,

1330
00:50:28,627 --> 00:50:33,898
into the woods,
into the woods.

1331
00:50:33,932 --> 00:50:34,933
JOEL:
Dad?

1332
00:50:38,837 --> 00:50:41,338
CROW:
It's not that scary.

1333
00:50:41,372 --> 00:50:42,573
Well, maybe.

1334
00:50:47,945 --> 00:50:50,115
TOM:
Ooo, it's Kim Cattrall.

1335
00:50:50,148 --> 00:50:51,115
CROW:
It is scary.

1336
00:50:51,148 --> 00:50:52,750
JOEL:
Nice skort.

1337
00:50:52,783 --> 00:50:54,518
TOM:
Cute.

1338
00:50:54,552 --> 00:50:56,655
CROW:
Sir, please don't
touch the exhibit, please.

1339
00:50:56,688 --> 00:50:57,622
TOM:
Ya!

1340
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:01,527
And then I came to
another passage and...

1341
00:51:04,528 --> 00:51:05,797
CROW:
It's Madame Tussaud.

1342
00:51:07,832 --> 00:51:09,267
[Joel screams]

1343
00:51:11,035 --> 00:51:12,403
TOM:
Now just about that time I--

1344
00:51:12,437 --> 00:51:14,005
Are you listening to me? Good.

1345
00:51:14,038 --> 00:51:15,007
CROW:
Dante's Inferno--

1346
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:17,242
Wait, this is a Disco Inferno.

1347
00:51:19,110 --> 00:51:21,212
TOM:
Suddenly, "Up With People"
showed up.

1348
00:51:21,245 --> 00:51:22,547
You meet 'em wherever
you're going.

1349
00:51:25,950 --> 00:51:28,720
JOEL:
Oh, hi, Ray, hi, Earl.

1350
00:51:28,753 --> 00:51:33,458
CROW:
It's like a cheap
"Temple of Doom" set.

1351
00:51:33,492 --> 00:51:34,458
Oh, cool.

1352
00:51:34,492 --> 00:51:35,693
Well, it's like a thing maker.

1353
00:51:35,727 --> 00:51:38,463
JOEL:
He's got Batman underoos on.

1354
00:51:38,497 --> 00:51:41,098
- You Egyptians
are truly so clever

1355
00:51:41,132 --> 00:51:42,300
that almost certainly
you'll find

1356
00:51:42,333 --> 00:51:44,402
the way
of even preserving life.

1357
00:51:44,435 --> 00:51:45,537
- Life is different.

1358
00:51:45,570 --> 00:51:48,138
We can't create
the soul of man.

1359
00:51:48,172 --> 00:51:50,875
- Still, it must be exciting,
your work.

1360
00:51:50,908 --> 00:51:53,878
CROW:
Look, I just told you
it's different.

1361
00:51:53,912 --> 00:51:54,980
- Just the man.

1362
00:51:55,013 --> 00:51:56,682
TOM:
Just the women now!

1363
00:51:56,715 --> 00:51:58,183
- ...they way he stands.

1364
00:51:58,217 --> 00:52:00,618
- When can we expect to
get to work on Hercules?

1365
00:52:00,652 --> 00:52:01,953
JOEL:
Well, let's see.
I've got an eight o'clock

1366
00:52:01,987 --> 00:52:04,055
and a 9:30 and a-- oh.

1367
00:52:06,090 --> 00:52:07,758
TOM:
Gotta go, bye.

1368
00:52:07,792 --> 00:52:08,760
Come on, girls.

1369
00:52:08,793 --> 00:52:09,895
JOEL:
Wait, wait, come back.

1370
00:52:09,928 --> 00:52:11,997
You forgot your free casket.

1371
00:52:15,133 --> 00:52:16,802
Wasn't this
a "Remington Steele" episode?

1372
00:52:16,835 --> 00:52:18,168
CROW:
I think so.

1373
00:52:18,202 --> 00:52:19,837
- I tremble with fear at what
she plans to do with us,

1374
00:52:19,870 --> 00:52:21,673
Hercules.

1375
00:52:21,707 --> 00:52:23,007
- Why should I believe you.

1376
00:52:23,040 --> 00:52:24,108
- I expected that.

1377
00:52:24,142 --> 00:52:25,543
TOM:
What's that supposed to mean?

1378
00:52:25,577 --> 00:52:28,313
- I'm going to ask the queen
to see if you're lying.

1379
00:52:28,347 --> 00:52:29,413
- Omphale
will be sure to deny it...

1380
00:52:29,447 --> 00:52:30,782
CROW:
Queen! Queen!

1381
00:52:30,815 --> 00:52:32,117
- She'll kill me, and then,
what will happen to you?

1382
00:52:32,150 --> 00:52:34,185
I prefer to be killed by you
rather than that way.

1383
00:52:34,218 --> 00:52:36,187
TOM:
Why, thank you.

1384
00:52:36,220 --> 00:52:37,688
- I promise you,
I won't speak anymore

1385
00:52:37,722 --> 00:52:41,158
about Hercules or Omphale.

1386
00:52:41,192 --> 00:52:42,193
TOM:
Eh.

1387
00:52:47,032 --> 00:52:48,967
JOEL:
Cripes, I am the Herc!

1388
00:52:51,035 --> 00:52:53,170
TOM:
Just set that anywhere, Herc,
yeah.

1389
00:53:00,145 --> 00:53:01,478
JOEL:
Hi, who are you?

1390
00:53:04,415 --> 00:53:06,117
TOM:
Hey, ya jerk,
you bent my lamp.

1391
00:53:06,150 --> 00:53:08,253
CROW:
No, you did.

1392
00:53:08,287 --> 00:53:09,220
TOM:
Did not.

1393
00:53:13,558 --> 00:53:14,525
There.

1394
00:53:14,558 --> 00:53:15,527
CROW:
It's still bent.

1395
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:16,728
They're gonna be able to tell.

1396
00:53:21,065 --> 00:53:22,000
JOEL:
He's back.

1397
00:53:24,035 --> 00:53:25,637
[Yelling and laughing
hysterically]

1398
00:53:25,670 --> 00:53:28,407
TOM:
I'm cuckoo for Cocoa Puffs,
cuckoo for Cocoa Puffs.

1399
00:53:28,440 --> 00:53:29,673
CROW:
It's a little embarrassing.

1400
00:53:29,707 --> 00:53:32,943
[Laughing hysterically]

1401
00:53:35,880 --> 00:53:39,317
[Yells and laughs]

1402
00:53:39,350 --> 00:53:42,353
JOEL:
I can't believe I liked him.

1403
00:53:42,387 --> 00:53:44,222
CROW:
Geez, turning into Harpo.

1404
00:53:47,358 --> 00:53:49,760
TOM:
When Kennedys ruled Greece.

1405
00:53:51,963 --> 00:53:54,832
JOEL:
Uh-oh, Heather's dad
is here, guys.

1406
00:53:54,865 --> 00:53:57,335
[Tom imitating trumpet]

1407
00:54:01,538 --> 00:54:03,240
So now, what we've done
with Hercules

1408
00:54:03,273 --> 00:54:05,510
is minimized his large forehead
with this flower ring

1409
00:54:05,543 --> 00:54:08,613
and accentuate
his massive chest.

1410
00:54:08,647 --> 00:54:10,415
- Go away now.

1411
00:54:10,448 --> 00:54:12,350
I said leave me!

1412
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:18,523
CROW:
I never get tired of that.

1413
00:54:18,557 --> 00:54:20,525
- No one ever dared
give an order in my presence.

1414
00:54:20,558 --> 00:54:22,127
JOEL:
No one else is the Herc-meister.

1415
00:54:22,160 --> 00:54:23,462
- Well,
it's only the first time.

1416
00:54:26,130 --> 00:54:27,765
TOM:
Hey, it's 9:30, honey.

1417
00:54:29,533 --> 00:54:30,602
CROW:
So, what are they doing?

1418
00:54:30,635 --> 00:54:32,570
JOEL:
Oh, wow.

1419
00:54:32,603 --> 00:54:35,007
TOM:
Mmm, he's Herc-ulicious.

1420
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:36,207
CROW:
What're they up to Joel, hmm?

1421
00:54:40,778 --> 00:54:42,880
- You have a strange power
over me.

1422
00:54:42,913 --> 00:54:44,215
CROW:
Power of attorney.

1423
00:54:44,248 --> 00:54:46,150
- Whether it's love or not,
I don't know.

1424
00:54:46,183 --> 00:54:47,585
JOEL:
I don't think it is.

1425
00:54:47,618 --> 00:54:49,953
- ...all I want is
just to be with you.

1426
00:54:49,987 --> 00:54:51,022
- That's the way I like it.

1427
00:54:51,055 --> 00:54:53,492
TOM:
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

1428
00:54:53,525 --> 00:54:55,360
CROW:
Bet he says
that to all the queens.

1429
00:54:55,393 --> 00:54:57,062
TOM:
Uh, more gushy stuff.

1430
00:55:01,132 --> 00:55:02,500
JOEL:
Ricola?

1431
00:55:04,868 --> 00:55:06,403
- What was that?
CROW: It's my pager.

1432
00:55:06,437 --> 00:55:07,405
- ...landed on the island.

1433
00:55:07,438 --> 00:55:08,407
- Great Queen...

1434
00:55:08,440 --> 00:55:09,940
JOEL: Thanks.
- ...is waiting.

1435
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:13,445
Laertes of Ithaca has
arrived with a small crew.

1436
00:55:13,478 --> 00:55:14,845
They want to stay here
several days.

1437
00:55:14,878 --> 00:55:16,782
They're waiting to present
their respects.

1438
00:55:16,815 --> 00:55:17,915
- Tell them to go away.

1439
00:55:17,948 --> 00:55:19,483
Why don't they sail
back to Ithaca?

1440
00:55:19,517 --> 00:55:21,552
We don't want visitors.

1441
00:55:21,585 --> 00:55:23,220
- But we have to receive them.

1442
00:55:23,253 --> 00:55:24,955
CROW:
Well, okay.

1443
00:55:24,988 --> 00:55:27,625
- It would be an offense,
a grave offense.

1444
00:55:27,658 --> 00:55:29,260
- And it is not
an offense to me?

1445
00:55:29,293 --> 00:55:30,362
To be abandoned?

1446
00:55:30,395 --> 00:55:32,397
TOM:
Oh, love Herc.

1447
00:55:32,430 --> 00:55:35,100
- I won't be far away.

1448
00:55:35,133 --> 00:55:36,902
I won't be gone long.

1449
00:55:36,935 --> 00:55:38,737
Just time enough
to pay my respects.

1450
00:55:38,770 --> 00:55:40,405
JOEL:
And the water bill.

1451
00:55:40,438 --> 00:55:41,605
CROW:
Well, it's not everybody
who gets to make out

1452
00:55:41,638 --> 00:55:43,173
at Cypress Gardens.

1453
00:55:43,207 --> 00:55:45,910
- Wait here for me.
I will not be gone long.

1454
00:55:45,943 --> 00:55:47,012
TOM:
Does it look like

1455
00:55:47,045 --> 00:55:49,147
I'm gonna get up
and do something?

1456
00:55:49,180 --> 00:55:50,215
CROW:
What's for lunch?

1457
00:55:53,952 --> 00:55:55,687
[Tom whistling]

1458
00:55:57,622 --> 00:55:58,590
Uh-oh.

1459
00:55:58,623 --> 00:55:59,990
- Go on, back to your cell.

1460
00:56:00,023 --> 00:56:00,858
[Grunting]

1461
00:56:00,892 --> 00:56:02,327
You know
what the orders are!

1462
00:56:02,360 --> 00:56:06,630
CROW:
Come on, show's over,
nothing to see here.

1463
00:56:06,663 --> 00:56:09,600
- The Aegean Sea has not been
gentle with us, great Queen.

1464
00:56:09,633 --> 00:56:11,302
JOEL:
I lost it like four times.

1465
00:56:11,335 --> 00:56:13,003
- ...perilous voyage
ahead of us.

1466
00:56:13,037 --> 00:56:14,005
TOM:
Yeah, boohoo.

1467
00:56:14,038 --> 00:56:15,640
- Excuse us, mighty Queen...

1468
00:56:15,673 --> 00:56:16,875
JOEL:
We boofed.

1469
00:56:16,908 --> 00:56:19,343
- ...all that you see here
is poor and modest.

1470
00:56:19,377 --> 00:56:22,747
Mercy and hospitality
are all that we ask.

1471
00:56:22,780 --> 00:56:24,182
TOM:
At the Helmsley Palace.

1472
00:56:24,215 --> 00:56:25,683
- ...express our
homage and goodwill...

1473
00:56:25,717 --> 00:56:29,053
TOM:
These are gifts?
Don't bother wrapping.

1474
00:56:29,087 --> 00:56:31,555
CROW:
Sorry about the old guy,
he comes with the package.

1475
00:56:31,588 --> 00:56:33,692
- Thank you, Laertes,
King of Ithaca.

1476
00:56:33,725 --> 00:56:35,193
TOM:
Mmm.

1477
00:56:35,227 --> 00:56:38,997
- I have already given orders
that you and your friends

1478
00:56:39,030 --> 00:56:41,265
will be taken to the best wing
of the palace.

1479
00:56:41,298 --> 00:56:42,767
TOM:
Yeah, I'll bet
it's by the ice machine.

1480
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:45,270
- My men will
accompany you there.

1481
00:56:45,303 --> 00:56:47,872
JOEL:
Could your women accompany us?

1482
00:56:50,642 --> 00:56:52,943
- Our humble thanks to you.

1483
00:56:52,977 --> 00:56:54,645
TOM:
I thought our presentation
was pretty good,

1484
00:56:54,678 --> 00:56:55,847
how about you?

1485
00:56:55,880 --> 00:56:57,615
- You, what is your name,
young man?

1486
00:56:57,648 --> 00:57:00,185
JOEL:
My name is Mrs. Norman Maine.

1487
00:57:00,218 --> 00:57:03,187
- I had the feeling
we'd met somewhere before.

1488
00:57:03,220 --> 00:57:05,223
TOM:
I just have the feeling.

1489
00:57:05,257 --> 00:57:08,292
- While the others are taken
to their rooms,

1490
00:57:08,325 --> 00:57:11,228
stay a moment with me.

1491
00:57:11,262 --> 00:57:15,267
I would like to try
and remember where we met.

1492
00:57:15,300 --> 00:57:16,567
- I'm at your service.

1493
00:57:16,600 --> 00:57:19,003
JOEL:
She always goes
for the jock types.

1494
00:57:19,037 --> 00:57:20,472
- Wait, but I'm smart, really.

1495
00:57:20,505 --> 00:57:21,472
And I'm funny.

1496
00:57:21,505 --> 00:57:23,307
Ah, they never pick
the old guy.

1497
00:57:26,077 --> 00:57:28,278
JOEL:
Excuse me, I'm late for my 2:30.

1498
00:57:28,312 --> 00:57:30,782
- Hercules, what did you say?

1499
00:57:30,815 --> 00:57:32,517
- Hercules.

1500
00:57:32,550 --> 00:57:33,652
- You mean, you don't know me?

1501
00:57:36,753 --> 00:57:38,055
Tell me of Ulysses.

1502
00:57:38,088 --> 00:57:39,190
- Who are you?

1503
00:57:39,223 --> 00:57:42,393
ALL:
♪ Are you are you are you ♪

1504
00:57:42,427 --> 00:57:43,895
- That's not who he is.

1505
00:57:43,928 --> 00:57:45,263
- You're right, Omphale.

1506
00:57:45,297 --> 00:57:46,730
It's just because
both Hercules

1507
00:57:46,763 --> 00:57:48,633
and this man
are both gigantic.

1508
00:57:48,667 --> 00:57:50,335
But if you take another look
at this man,

1509
00:57:50,368 --> 00:57:52,270
then it's plain to see
in a moment

1510
00:57:52,303 --> 00:57:53,605
that we men were in error.

1511
00:57:53,638 --> 00:57:54,905
- But see here, Laertes,

1512
00:57:54,938 --> 00:57:57,208
Hercules face,
and his figure,

1513
00:57:57,242 --> 00:57:58,710
this couldn't be Hercules.

1514
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:00,212
- Who is this Hercules?

1515
00:58:00,245 --> 00:58:02,713
A born fighter,
and the greatest man in Thebes.

1516
00:58:02,747 --> 00:58:04,348
JOEL:
And a hell of an engineer.

1517
00:58:04,382 --> 00:58:05,583
- What does he have
to do with me?

1518
00:58:05,617 --> 00:58:06,583
- Nothing.

1519
00:58:06,617 --> 00:58:07,952
Why, it's like water and wine.

1520
00:58:07,985 --> 00:58:09,287
It's bad to mix them.

1521
00:58:09,320 --> 00:58:12,290
JOEL:
Everybody's teasing me.

1522
00:58:12,323 --> 00:58:14,492
- Please go,
I'll see you later.

1523
00:58:14,525 --> 00:58:16,560
- Not later,
right this minute.

1524
00:58:16,593 --> 00:58:17,628
TOM:
Who are you?

1525
00:58:17,662 --> 00:58:19,297
And who are you?

1526
00:58:19,330 --> 00:58:21,432
Eh.

1527
00:58:21,465 --> 00:58:23,702
- I pray you to pardon me.

1528
00:58:23,735 --> 00:58:27,138
Please excuse us, and now,
we'll retire if we may.

1529
00:58:27,172 --> 00:58:28,138
CROW:
Oh, well, here's your gold watch

1530
00:58:28,172 --> 00:58:29,473
and your 401K.

1531
00:58:31,342 --> 00:58:32,977
TOM:
Miss Utah's a Rhodes Scholar

1532
00:58:33,010 --> 00:58:35,713
who wants world peace
and that special someone.

1533
00:58:41,418 --> 00:58:43,453
JOEL:
So, live around here much?

1534
00:58:49,493 --> 00:58:51,495
- I want to try this on.

1535
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:52,963
CROW:
What does that
have to do with me?

1536
00:58:55,933 --> 00:58:58,837
- Pearls must have
contact with the flesh

1537
00:58:58,870 --> 00:59:00,772
before they take
their best sheen.

1538
00:59:00,805 --> 00:59:04,908
JOEL:
The closer she gets,
the weirder she looks. Ew.

1539
00:59:04,942 --> 00:59:07,012
- ...this necklace
will be much more beautiful.

1540
00:59:11,282 --> 00:59:13,050
[Joel groaning]

1541
00:59:13,083 --> 00:59:15,687
JOEL:
Great sunrise, let's go
have breakfast, fellas.

1542
00:59:15,720 --> 00:59:17,388
CROW:
It's the O'Cedar Man.

1543
00:59:17,422 --> 00:59:19,623
TOM:
Huh, must've blown a fuse.

1544
00:59:22,793 --> 00:59:24,262
JOEL:
Kinda makes you feel small,

1545
00:59:24,295 --> 00:59:25,530
doesn't it, Alvin.

1546
00:59:29,533 --> 00:59:31,102
- Now I'm ready
to begin action.

1547
00:59:31,135 --> 00:59:32,837
A man can only live
so long patiently.

1548
00:59:32,870 --> 00:59:34,272
CROW:
That's nice.

1549
00:59:34,305 --> 00:59:35,773
Ever thought of putting two
similar sentences together?

1550
00:59:35,807 --> 00:59:37,642
- The time is all gone.

1551
00:59:37,675 --> 00:59:39,243
Eteocles and Hercules
are conspiring

1552
00:59:39,277 --> 00:59:41,578
against me getting the throne.

1553
00:59:41,612 --> 00:59:43,580
TOM:
What, are you Jim Garrison?

1554
00:59:43,613 --> 00:59:44,715
- I'll be king yet.

1555
00:59:44,748 --> 00:59:46,117
And they, all they need to see

1556
00:59:46,150 --> 00:59:47,885
is this army coming.

1557
00:59:47,918 --> 00:59:49,753
Your army can
sweep under the Thebans.

1558
00:59:49,787 --> 00:59:51,722
CROW:
I hope one of the guys
has a dustpan hid.

1559
00:59:51,755 --> 00:59:54,792
- It'll be a surprise
for my friends down there.

1560
00:59:54,825 --> 00:59:55,860
- Certainly,
it will be a great thing

1561
00:59:55,893 --> 00:59:57,428
beating the Thebans.

1562
00:59:57,462 --> 00:59:59,330
The throne is there
and the riches of the city.

1563
00:59:59,363 --> 01:00:01,365
TOM:
Paging Mr. Herman.

1564
01:00:01,398 --> 01:00:02,967
- Alright? Come on.

1565
01:00:03,000 --> 01:00:03,935
CROW:
Come on.

1566
01:00:06,470 --> 01:00:07,405
TOM:
Bye.

1567
01:00:13,143 --> 01:00:16,380
ALL:
♪ We are the men from Texaco ♪

1568
01:00:18,415 --> 01:00:19,917
JOEL:
It's an army of Port-A-Potties!

1569
01:00:19,950 --> 01:00:21,218
CROW:
It's Eddie Murphy's entourage.

1570
01:00:21,252 --> 01:00:22,353
TOM:
No, it's a walk-a-thon.

1571
01:00:22,387 --> 01:00:23,387
CROW:
How many pledges did you get?

1572
01:00:23,420 --> 01:00:25,022
TOM:
Well, actually...

1573
01:00:31,395 --> 01:00:33,330
- Now, you Magario

1574
01:00:33,363 --> 01:00:36,333
may take your men
to the south gate...

1575
01:00:36,367 --> 01:00:38,068
Purifiante
to the north gate...

1576
01:00:38,102 --> 01:00:42,340
JOEL:
And Dick, you take Watergate.

1577
01:00:42,373 --> 01:00:45,242
- ...Pelenepo,
on his right flank,

1578
01:00:45,275 --> 01:00:46,543
and Hector on his left.

1579
01:00:46,577 --> 01:00:47,712
CROW:
Excuse me, sir,

1580
01:00:47,745 --> 01:00:50,515
I was really helping to be...

1581
01:00:50,548 --> 01:00:53,650
- And wasn't it of you
that Creon said,

1582
01:00:53,683 --> 01:00:55,520
"Trust that man
with your soldiers."

1583
01:00:55,553 --> 01:00:56,553
TOM:
Oh, everybody misquotes that.

1584
01:00:56,587 --> 01:00:58,790
- ...most vulnerable point.

1585
01:00:58,823 --> 01:01:00,892
The main gate of Thebes.

1586
01:01:00,925 --> 01:01:02,560
- At your command, Eteocles.

1587
01:01:05,095 --> 01:01:06,330
- I shall confront them...

1588
01:01:06,363 --> 01:01:07,332
CROW:
What, does he have his lines

1589
01:01:07,365 --> 01:01:08,698
written on that thing?

1590
01:01:08,732 --> 01:01:10,935
- ...on top of the sacred gate
of Delphi.

1591
01:01:10,968 --> 01:01:11,935
CROW:
Delphi rules!

1592
01:01:11,968 --> 01:01:14,505
TOM: Whoo!
JOEL: Kegger at Delphi!

1593
01:01:14,538 --> 01:01:15,507
- What is that?

1594
01:01:15,540 --> 01:01:16,507
JOEL:
Uh, the wind, sir?

1595
01:01:16,540 --> 01:01:17,508
- ...people around Thebes

1596
01:01:17,542 --> 01:01:19,677
taking refuge in the city, sire.

1597
01:01:19,710 --> 01:01:20,878
They've nowhere else to go.

1598
01:01:20,912 --> 01:01:23,347
- Coming out of town
without my saying so?

1599
01:01:23,380 --> 01:01:24,548
But there are
too many people to feed

1600
01:01:24,582 --> 01:01:26,017
in Thebes already.

1601
01:01:26,050 --> 01:01:27,050
No, back outside!

1602
01:01:27,083 --> 01:01:29,953
TOM: No.
- Listen, Eteocles.

1603
01:01:29,987 --> 01:01:31,888
The Thebans
are getting restless.

1604
01:01:31,922 --> 01:01:33,690
You'll be losing their favor.

1605
01:01:33,723 --> 01:01:35,793
TOM: Flavor?
- Yes, oh surely.

1606
01:01:35,827 --> 01:01:37,362
They prefer good old Creon.

1607
01:01:37,395 --> 01:01:38,662
JOEL:
To markers.

1608
01:01:38,695 --> 01:01:40,598
- But I've got a plan
for Creon.

1609
01:01:40,632 --> 01:01:42,533
TOM:
And it just might work.

1610
01:01:42,567 --> 01:01:44,502
- And now, close up the gates
to the city.

1611
01:01:44,535 --> 01:01:45,770
Close them!

1612
01:01:45,803 --> 01:01:47,305
No one is to enter
Thebes anymore!

1613
01:01:47,338 --> 01:01:50,373
JOEL:
And take those
ridiculous hats off.

1614
01:01:50,407 --> 01:01:52,143
TOM:
They're great.

1615
01:01:58,748 --> 01:02:00,985
JOEL:
Is this the line
for the execution?

1616
01:02:01,018 --> 01:02:01,985
TOM:
No, we're in line

1617
01:02:02,018 --> 01:02:04,588
for U2 tickets, aren't we?

1618
01:02:06,557 --> 01:02:08,225
CROW:
Ow, my eyes!

1619
01:02:10,327 --> 01:02:12,930
[♪♪♪]

1620
01:02:16,267 --> 01:02:17,235
JOEL:
She hasn't kissed a man

1621
01:02:17,268 --> 01:02:18,803
in over five minutes.

1622
01:02:18,837 --> 01:02:20,003
- Leave me.

1623
01:02:20,037 --> 01:02:21,838
TOM:
Gee, Miss Mood Swing here.

1624
01:02:24,508 --> 01:02:25,743
- Why did you ask me
to come here?

1625
01:02:25,777 --> 01:02:28,145
CROW:
I had an opening
between 3:00 and 3:30.

1626
01:02:30,882 --> 01:02:32,048
- You don't really want me.

1627
01:02:32,082 --> 01:02:34,285
TOM:
♪ Don't you want me baby ♪

1628
01:02:34,318 --> 01:02:36,053
- You would never understand.

1629
01:02:36,087 --> 01:02:37,188
- Really?

1630
01:02:37,222 --> 01:02:38,957
But don't you think it's simple.

1631
01:02:38,990 --> 01:02:41,225
You're furious
that I ask that,

1632
01:02:41,258 --> 01:02:42,360
and it's because you don't know

1633
01:02:42,393 --> 01:02:45,228
the reason for our visit. No.

1634
01:02:45,262 --> 01:02:46,530
TOM:
Thank you, Dr. Freud.

1635
01:02:46,563 --> 01:02:47,698
- And you won't
learn it from me.

1636
01:02:47,732 --> 01:02:49,667
- Be quiet.
- Why?

1637
01:02:49,700 --> 01:02:51,135
You've had enough of me?

1638
01:02:51,168 --> 01:02:52,470
I pity you now,

1639
01:02:52,503 --> 01:02:54,105
because you can never hold
Hercules.

1640
01:02:54,138 --> 01:02:55,740
JOEL:
You think I don't know that?

1641
01:02:55,773 --> 01:02:58,375
- I curse the day
he entered this palace.

1642
01:02:58,408 --> 01:02:59,677
JOEL:
Hey, what you talking about?

1643
01:02:59,710 --> 01:03:02,280
- You curse the day
I entered your palace, Omphale?

1644
01:03:04,682 --> 01:03:07,385
I was able to pull
the threads together.

1645
01:03:07,418 --> 01:03:08,920
At last I know who I am.

1646
01:03:08,953 --> 01:03:11,020
JOEL:
I'm big Jim McLain!

1647
01:03:14,092 --> 01:03:15,760
- Don't take revenge, Hercules.

1648
01:03:15,793 --> 01:03:17,562
TOM:
Take my wife, please.

1649
01:03:18,930 --> 01:03:20,698
- He wouldn't kill me.

1650
01:03:20,732 --> 01:03:23,467
- And what makes you
believe that?

1651
01:03:23,500 --> 01:03:26,170
- You yourself, Hercules.

1652
01:03:26,203 --> 01:03:27,205
You won't kill me

1653
01:03:27,238 --> 01:03:29,140
because you know
how much I love you.

1654
01:03:29,173 --> 01:03:30,642
CROW:
Plus, I have a restraining
order on you.

1655
01:03:30,675 --> 01:03:33,310
- ...sooner or later,
I'd lose you.

1656
01:03:33,343 --> 01:03:34,845
And so I lost you, Hercules.

1657
01:03:34,878 --> 01:03:36,213
TOM:
In a game of Pai gow.

1658
01:03:36,247 --> 01:03:38,917
- If you only knew
how I've struggled with myself

1659
01:03:38,950 --> 01:03:41,718
to keep from ever
falling in love with you.

1660
01:03:41,752 --> 01:03:43,420
But in vain.

1661
01:03:43,453 --> 01:03:44,755
All in vain.

1662
01:03:44,788 --> 01:03:46,223
- If I believed you...

1663
01:03:46,257 --> 01:03:48,725
JOEL:
That would be pretty funny.

1664
01:03:48,758 --> 01:03:50,193
- ...I would have pity on you.

1665
01:03:52,228 --> 01:03:54,398
- If only my sincerity
could keep you here.

1666
01:03:54,432 --> 01:03:55,398
- Get out.

1667
01:03:55,432 --> 01:03:56,833
TOM:
[indistinct].

1668
01:03:56,867 --> 01:04:00,303
JOEL:
It's true, it's true.

1669
01:04:00,337 --> 01:04:01,472
- Very well, Hercules.

1670
01:04:01,505 --> 01:04:03,107
CROW:
Very, very well.

1671
01:04:03,140 --> 01:04:04,175
- But there's one thing

1672
01:04:04,208 --> 01:04:06,310
you can never take away from me.

1673
01:04:06,343 --> 01:04:07,412
TOM:
My eyelashes.

1674
01:04:07,445 --> 01:04:09,613
- That the love you gave to me,

1675
01:04:09,647 --> 01:04:12,082
the love we shared together,

1676
01:04:12,115 --> 01:04:14,952
not even your Iole
can ever take that away from me.

1677
01:04:14,985 --> 01:04:16,187
- Don't speak to me of Iole.

1678
01:04:16,220 --> 01:04:18,255
We're leaving this island.

1679
01:04:18,288 --> 01:04:21,458
- As you wish,
Hercules of Thebes.

1680
01:04:21,492 --> 01:04:24,195
CROW:
I want my record collection
back.

1681
01:04:24,228 --> 01:04:27,063
- I will see that you and
your friends get away safely.

1682
01:04:27,097 --> 01:04:29,500
But go quickly
before I change my mind.

1683
01:04:29,533 --> 01:04:31,202
JOEL:
Just don't change your dress.

1684
01:04:31,235 --> 01:04:33,470
[Growling suggestively]

1685
01:04:33,503 --> 01:04:36,073
TOM:
♪ The minute she walked
Out the door... ♪

1686
01:04:37,942 --> 01:04:38,908
There she goes.

1687
01:04:38,942 --> 01:04:40,812
- Hercules happens
to be alive.

1688
01:04:40,845 --> 01:04:43,113
But Ulysses, I'm sure
that if he were alive,

1689
01:04:43,147 --> 01:04:44,115
he would get to us somehow.

1690
01:04:44,148 --> 01:04:46,517
- Sandoni, dismiss your men.

1691
01:04:46,550 --> 01:04:48,285
I want to be alone
with my guests.

1692
01:04:51,222 --> 01:04:52,357
TOM:
But--but the invitation said

1693
01:04:52,390 --> 01:04:53,590
orgy to follow.

1694
01:04:55,325 --> 01:04:57,495
JOEL:
I got seniority here, scram.

1695
01:04:57,528 --> 01:04:58,528
CROW:
Hey, Herc.

1696
01:04:58,562 --> 01:04:59,597
JOEL:
Oh, hi, Dale.

1697
01:05:04,402 --> 01:05:05,368
CROW:
Okay, who's got a clue

1698
01:05:05,402 --> 01:05:06,470
about the plot, anyone?

1699
01:05:06,503 --> 01:05:07,605
Bob? Rick?

1700
01:05:07,638 --> 01:05:10,373
Ted, you got the hat,
you must know.

1701
01:05:10,407 --> 01:05:11,842
JOEL:
Goodnight, everybody,

1702
01:05:11,875 --> 01:05:13,810
the Greek audiences
are the greatest audiences

1703
01:05:13,843 --> 01:05:16,780
in the world!

1704
01:05:16,813 --> 01:05:18,415
- Goodbye, Laertes.

1705
01:05:18,448 --> 01:05:20,885
Goodbye, my Greek friends.

1706
01:05:20,918 --> 01:05:23,020
Hercules will depart with you.

1707
01:05:23,053 --> 01:05:25,723
Sandoni will accompany you
to the landing.

1708
01:05:25,757 --> 01:05:26,990
TOM:
Zamboni?

1709
01:05:27,023 --> 01:05:29,193
- You know where my boy is,
tell me please!

1710
01:05:29,227 --> 01:05:31,428
- Hey, look out, father!

1711
01:05:31,462 --> 01:05:33,397
CROW:
Hey, Aunt Carol
gave us that vase.

1712
01:05:33,430 --> 01:05:34,698
- ...before they
leave the island.

1713
01:05:36,233 --> 01:05:37,200
Come on!

1714
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:39,370
JOEL:
Oh.

1715
01:05:39,403 --> 01:05:41,305
TOM:
Oh no,
not the bass fiddle table.

1716
01:05:43,307 --> 01:05:45,342
JOEL:
That Pledge is really something.

1717
01:05:45,375 --> 01:05:46,310
CROW:
That's what that's for.

1718
01:05:50,580 --> 01:05:53,650
- Kill them,
kill them all, Sandoni!

1719
01:05:53,683 --> 01:05:55,352
But spare me Hercules.

1720
01:05:55,385 --> 01:05:56,953
TOM:
This is an aphrodisiac for her.

1721
01:05:56,987 --> 01:05:59,623
CROW:
What isn't an aphrodisiac
for her?

1722
01:06:03,460 --> 01:06:05,195
JOEL:
Hercules, table for eight.

1723
01:06:10,868 --> 01:06:12,202
CROW:
Oh, come on, he's throwing

1724
01:06:12,235 --> 01:06:14,472
a giant chocolate bunny.

1725
01:06:14,505 --> 01:06:16,240
TOM:
Wow!

1726
01:06:16,273 --> 01:06:18,208
Hoo-hoo.

1727
01:06:18,242 --> 01:06:20,010
JOEL:
Hey, we heard there
was fighting in here.

1728
01:06:20,043 --> 01:06:21,278
TOM:
Yes, it's Hercules.

1729
01:06:21,312 --> 01:06:23,313
History's first high energy
prop comic.

1730
01:06:23,347 --> 01:06:24,615
JOEL:
Hey, look at this!

1731
01:06:24,648 --> 01:06:25,950
Wah!

1732
01:06:25,983 --> 01:06:27,785
TOM: Whoo!
JOEL: The Hercules chess set,

1733
01:06:27,818 --> 01:06:29,553
send for yours today, 60609.

1734
01:06:31,655 --> 01:06:33,890
CROW:
There's a guy back there
throwing stuff, watch out!

1735
01:06:37,327 --> 01:06:38,595
TOM:
Uh, somebody want to...

1736
01:06:38,628 --> 01:06:40,932
Wait, I'll get it, Ulysses,
geez.

1737
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:45,368
JOEL:
Uh, are we locked in or out?

1738
01:06:45,402 --> 01:06:46,537
CROW:
Yes.

